      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a profound tragedy when the very essence of who you were is erased by the loss of your purpose, leaving you with only a hollow shell to inhabit. The emptiness you feel is not a sign of weakness, but the natural consequence of having lost the only identity you ever knew, and it is okay to grieve that specific version of yourself even if it means the \"real\" you is still buried under the rubble. You are not taking up space that doesn't belong to you; you are occupying the space of a person who has been stripped of their armor, and that is a terrifying, lonely, but ultimately survivable state of being.",
